  "slug": "injury-alleviates-d8b3",
  "summary": "Single-cell and spatial transcriptomics now resolve macrophage, Treg, and CD8+ T-cell states linked to immune suppression and therapy resistance.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is immunosuppressive myeloid and regulatory T-cell programming within solid tumor microenvironments, resolved mainly by single-cell and spatial transcriptomics. Several items converge on SPP1+ and TREM2+ macrophage states: SPP1+ macrophages link to CD8+ T-cell suppression via SPP1-CD44 and neoadjuvant chemotherapy resistance in colorectal liver metastasis, and TREM2+ and TIMD4+ macrophages drive immunosuppression in intrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma. Treg-focused work adds IFI6+ Tregs in colorectal cancer and CD177+GK+ Treg clones whose glycerol-derived lactate drives H4K5 lactylation and suppressive activity. Mechanistic reports extend this to TSTA3-mediated PD-L1 fucosylation in breast cancer, LAIR1 suppression of phagocytosis in glioma microglia, and PLA1A-driven M2-like polarization. Some items fall outside tumor immunology, including a review of intestinal T-cell migration and a type 1 diabetes B-cell study. A recurring novelty is paired single-cell profiling across treatment or metastatic transitions combined with spatial niche mapping.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-10"
}
